    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "e0e0992d8a0664437e06e2e13077dcc83136cc621b54e0012e84cc4db4874b8e",
      "text": "Duration: 8 Hours • Pick Up: 9:00–9:30 am • Language: English and Spanish. Visit Monte Albán (UNESCO), the mountaintop Zapotec ceremonial city, exploring temples, pyramids, ball courts, and tombs with expert storytelling. Continue to San Antonio Arrazola to see hand-carved and painted alebrijes, then to San Bartolo Coyotepec for a black clay pottery workshop visit. Included: Shared transportation, certified bilingual guide, entry to Monte Albán, artisan workshop visits, overnight in Oaxaca. Not included: Meals, tips, personal expenses.",
